{"t":"2026-05-28T02:56:16.166Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1ufiJKjm32ZZXaMwsXK6J","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# HYPHA-TESTS\n     2→\n     3→> HYPHA tag: `TA/TESTS`\n     4→> Maps to Mycelium agent: `tests-agent`\n     5→\n     6→## Goal\n     7→\n     8→Own the test suites for all iter-4 biomes. Every new path must have coverage. The test biome runs last in the cultivation wave, validating that all seams are properly closed.\n     9→\n    10→## Scope\n    11→\n    12→### In Scope\n    13→\n    14→- `tests/discovery/test_orchestrator_pubsub.py` — verify 8+ event sequence from `DiscoveryOrchestrator.run`\n    15→- `tests/scheduler/test_daily_task.py` — verify Celery task creates `crawl_runs` row, handles retries\n    16→- `tests/api/test_events_stream.py` — verify SSE endpoint streams events, sends heartbeats\n    17→- `tests/api/test_review_approve.py` — full integration: create application → approve → verify state transition\n    18→- `frontend/src/api/__tests__/client.test.ts` — vitest tests for auth header injection, 401 handling, error normalization\n    19→\n    20→### Out of Scope\n    21→\n    22→- E2E tests with Playwright (follow-up iteration)\n    23→- Load testing / performance benchmarks\n    24→- Coverage for frozen biomes (already tested)\n    25→- Frontend component tests (unit tests only for API client)\n    26→- Contract testing between frontend and backend\n    27→\n    28→## Inputs\n    29→\n    30→- `discover-agent`: `DiscoveryOrchestrator` class\n    31→- `scheduler-agent`: `daily_discovery_task` Celery task\n    32→- `api-streaming-agent`: `GET /events/stream` endpoint\n    33→- `api-agent`: `POST /applications/{id}/approve`, `POST /applications/{id}/reject` endpoints\n    34→- `api-client-agent`: `apiClient` and API wrapper functions\n    35→\n    36→## Outputs (Deliverables)\n    37→\n    38→- `tests/discovery/test_orchestrator_pubsub.py`\n    39→- `tests/scheduler/__init__.py`\n    40→- `tests/scheduler/test_daily_task.py`\n    41→- `tests/api/test_events_stream.py`\n    42→- `tests/api/test_review_approve.py`\n    43→- `frontend/src/api/__tests__/client.test.ts`\n    44→\n    45→## Acceptance Criteria\n    46→\n    47→### Backend (pytest)\n    48→\n    49→- [ ] `pytest tests/discovery/test_orchestrator_pubsub.py -v` passes\n    50→- [ ] Test uses `fakeredis.aioredis` for Redis — no real Redis required\n    51→- [ ] Test uses in-memory SQLite for database\n    52→- [ ] Asserts 8+ events in sequence: `RUN_STARTED, CANDIDATE_LOADED, PROFILE_BUILT, MANIFEST_BUILT, CRAWL_SOURCE_COMPLETE×4, CRAWL_COMPLETE, SCORING_COMPLETE, RUN_COMPLETE`\n    53→- [ ] Asserts no duplicate events\n    54→- [ ] Asserts `event=RUN_COMPLETE` is last\n    55→\n    56→- [ ] `pytest tests/scheduler/test_daily_task.py -v` passes\n    57→- [ ] Test mocks `DiscoveryOrchestrator` to avoid real Claude calls\n    58→- [ ] Asserts one `crawl_runs` row created per candidate\n    59→- [ ] Asserts idempotent re-fire deduplicates by `task_id`\n    60→- [ ] Asserts retry failure writes to `crawl_runs.error_log`\n    61→\n    62→- [ ] `pytest tests/api/test_events_stream.py -v` passes\n    63→- [ ] Test uses FastAPI `TestClient` with streaming response\n    64→- [ ] Publishes to Redis from test, asserts SSE frame surfaces\n    65→- [ ] Asserts `:ping` heartbeat within 16s\n    66→- [ ] Asserts 401 on missing auth\n    67→\n    68→- [ ] `pytest tests/api/test_review_approve.py -v` passes\n    69→- [ ] Creates application row in test database\n    70→- [ ] POSTs approve, asserts state transition to `APPROVED`\n    71→- [ ] Asserts `application_events` row written\n    72→- [ ] Asserts 404 on non-existent pipeline\n    73→- [ ] Asserts 400 on approving non-AWAITING_REVIEW pipeline\n    74→\n    75→### Frontend (vitest)\n    76→\n    77→- [ ] `cd frontend && npm test -- --run` passes\n    78→- [ ] `client.test.ts` mocks `fetch` via `vi.mock` or `msw`\n    79→- [ ] Asserts `Authorization: Bearer` header injected on requests\n    80→- [ ] Asserts 401 response triggers logout callback\n    81→- [ ] Asserts network error surfaces `TalentAgentApiError` with correct shape\n    82→\n    83→### Coverage\n    84→\n    85→- [ ] `pytest --cov=backend --cov-report=term-missing` shows ≥80% on new files\n    86→- [ ] Excludes `__init__.py` and migrations from coverage calculation\n    87→\n    88→### Linting\n    89→\n    90→- [ ] `ruff check backend/` clean\n    91→- [ ] `ruff check tests/` clean\n    92→\n    93→## Notes\n    94→\n    95→- Use `fakeredis.aioredis` for async Redis mocking. It supports pub/sub operations.\n    96→- Use `pytest-asyncio` for async test functions. Mark all async tests with `@pytest.mark.asyncio`.\n    97→- The in-memory SQLite setup is in `tests/conftest.py`. Reuse the existing fixtures.\n    98→- For SSE testing, `TestClient` with `stream=True` allows reading the response incrementally. Set a timeout to avoid hanging on heartbeat tests.\n    99→- The scheduler tests should mock `DiscoveryOrchestrator` at the import level to prevent real Claude API calls.\n   100→- Frontend tests use `vitest`. The `vi.mock` API is similar to Jest's `jest.mock`.\n   101→- Coverage threshold of 80% applies to new files only. Do not regress coverage on existing code.\n   102→- All test files must pass `ruff check` — no linting exceptions for test code.\n   103→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2750489-d8d6-41f5-b42f-4d2a4cab3a05","uuid":"eed4d026-02c9-4441-a11a-0c2a0f1b8e31","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/hyphae/HYPHA-TESTS.md","content":"# HYPHA-TESTS\n\n> HYPHA tag: `TA/TESTS`\n> Maps to Mycelium agent: `tests-agent`\n\n## Goal\n\nOwn the test suites for all iter-4 biomes. Every new path must have coverage. The test biome runs last in the cultivation wave, validating that all seams are properly closed.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n\n- `tests/discovery/test_orchestrator_pubsub.py` — verify 8+ event sequence from `DiscoveryOrchestrator.run`\n- `tests/scheduler/test_daily_task.py` — verify Celery task creates `crawl_runs` row, handles retries\n- `tests/api/test_events_stream.py` — verify SSE endpoint streams events, sends heartbeats\n- `tests/api/test_review_approve.py` — full integration: create application → approve → verify state transition\n- `frontend/src/api/__tests__/client.test.ts` — vitest tests for auth header injection, 401 handling, error normalization\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- E2E tests with Playwright (follow-up iteration)\n- Load testing / performance benchmarks\n- Coverage for frozen biomes (already tested)\n- Frontend component tests (unit tests only for API client)\n- Contract testing between frontend and backend\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `discover-agent`: `DiscoveryOrchestrator` class\n- `scheduler-agent`: `daily_discovery_task` Celery task\n- `api-streaming-agent`: `GET /events/stream` endpoint\n- `api-agent`: `POST /applications/{id}/approve`, `POST /applications/{id}/reject` endpoints\n- `api-client-agent`: `apiClient` and API wrapper functions\n\n## Outputs (Deliverables)\n\n- `tests/discovery/test_orchestrator_pubsub.py`\n- `tests/scheduler/__init__.py`\n- `tests/scheduler/test_daily_task.py`\n- `tests/api/test_events_stream.py`\n- `tests/api/test_review_approve.py`\n- `frontend/src/api/__tests__/client.test.ts`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Backend (pytest)\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/discovery/test_orchestrator_pubsub.py -v` passes\n- [ ] Test uses `fakeredis.aioredis` for Redis — no real Redis required\n- [ ] Test uses in-memory SQLite for database\n- [ ] Asserts 8+ events in sequence: `RUN_STARTED, CANDIDATE_LOADED, PROFILE_BUILT, MANIFEST_BUILT, CRAWL_SOURCE_COMPLETE×4, CRAWL_COMPLETE, SCORING_COMPLETE, RUN_COMPLETE`\n- [ ] Asserts no duplicate events\n- [ ] Asserts `event=RUN_COMPLETE` is last\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/scheduler/test_daily_task.py -v` passes\n- [ ] Test mocks `DiscoveryOrchestrator` to avoid real Claude calls\n- [ ] Asserts one `crawl_runs` row created per candidate\n- [ ] Asserts idempotent re-fire deduplicates by `task_id`\n- [ ] Asserts retry failure writes to `crawl_runs.error_log`\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/api/test_events_stream.py -v` passes\n- [ ] Test uses FastAPI `TestClient` with streaming response\n- [ ] Publishes to Redis from test, asserts SSE frame surfaces\n- [ ] Asserts `:ping` heartbeat within 16s\n- [ ] Asserts 401 on missing auth\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/api/test_review_approve.py -v` passes\n- [ ] Creates application row in test database\n- [ ] POSTs approve, asserts state transition to `APPROVED`\n- [ ] Asserts `application_events` row written\n- [ ] Asserts 404 on non-existent pipeline\n- [ ] Asserts 400 on approving non-AWAITING_REVIEW pipeline\n\n### Frontend (vitest)\n\n- [ ] `cd frontend && npm test -- --run` passes\n- [ ] `client.test.ts` mocks `fetch` via `vi.mock` or `msw`\n- [ ] Asserts `Authorization: Bearer` header injected on requests\n- [ ] Asserts 401 response triggers logout callback\n- [ ] Asserts network error surfaces `TalentAgentApiError` with correct shape\n\n### Coverage\n\n- [ ] `pytest --cov=backend --cov-report=term-missing` shows ≥80% on new files\n- [ ] Excludes `__init__.py` and migrations from coverage calculation\n\n### Linting\n\n- [ ] `ruff check backend/` clean\n- [ ] `ruff check tests/` clean\n\n## Notes\n\n- Use `fakeredis.aioredis` for async Redis mocking. It supports pub/sub operations.\n- Use `pytest-asyncio` for async test functions. Mark all async tests with `@pytest.mark.asyncio`.\n- The in-memory SQLite setup is in `tests/conftest.py`. Reuse the existing fixtures.\n- For SSE testing, `TestClient` with `stream=True` allows reading the response incrementally. Set a timeout to avoid hanging on heartbeat tests.\n- The scheduler tests should mock `DiscoveryOrchestrator` at the import level to prevent real Claude API calls.\n- Frontend tests use `vitest`. The `vi.mock` API is similar to Jest's `jest.mock`.\n- Coverage threshold of 80% applies to new files only. Do not regress coverage on existing code.\n- All test files must pass `ruff check` — no linting exceptions for test code.\n","numLines":103,"startLine":1,"totalLines":103}}}}
